1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,864
Nobody clapped. Not a single person in this crowded subway station cared about my broken guitar.

2
00:00:07,164 --> 00:00:13,668
Then I found the silver badge on the bench. No instructions, just a single pulsing red light.

3
00:00:13,968 --> 00:00:20,736
I pinned it to my lapel, struck a clumsy chord, and the world completely shattered around me.

4
00:00:21,036 --> 00:00:30,804
Thunderous cheers exploded from empty platforms. Hundreds of invisible hands clapped in a deafening, frantic rhythm.

5
00:00:31,104 --> 00:00:38,976
I played faster. The roar grew louder, feeding my desperate soul the validation I always craved.

6
00:00:39,276 --> 00:00:48,612
Every stranger I passed smiled and bowed, caught in the invisible wave of absolute, unearned adoration.

7
00:00:48,912 --> 00:00:56,280
Until the battery indicator blinked red, and the roaring applause suddenly began to sound remarkably familiar.

8
00:00:56,580 --> 00:01:03,564
It wasn't a crowd cheering. It was my own heartbeat, amplified and bounced back through the speakers.

9
00:01:03,864 --> 00:01:09,936
The badge wasn't measuring my talent. It was stealing my life force to pay for the applause.

10
00:01:10,236 --> 00:01:18,972
The music stopped. The cheers vanished. When the silence returns, will anyone be left to listen?
